COMMENTS OF NORTHERN VIRGINIA ELECTRIC COOPERATIVE, INC. 
Pursuant to paragraph 87 of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission’s (“FERC” or 
the “Commission”) February 20, 2025 Order Instituting Proceeding Under Section 206 of the 
Federal Power Act and Consolidating with Other Proceedings (“Show Cause Order”), Northern 
Virginia Electric Cooperative, Inc. (“NOVEC”)1 respectfully submits these comments 
addressing: “(1) whether the existing Tariff remains just and reasonable and not unduly 
discriminatory or preferential; and (2) if not, what changes to the Tariff should be implemented 
as replacement rates.”2 PJM Interconnection, L.L.C.’s (“PJM”) existing Open Access 

1 NOVEC filed its intervention in Docket No. EL25-49-000 on March 4, 2025. NOVEC, Motion to Intervene, Docket 
No. EL25-49-000 (filed March 4, 2025) (Accession No. 20250304-5077). 
2 PJM Interconnection, L.L.C., 190 FERC ¶ 61,115, P 87 (2025) (“Show Cause Order”) (“Interested entities may 
respond within 30 days of PJM’s and the Transmission Owners’ filings, addressing either or both of: (1) whether the 
existing Tariff remains just and reasonable and not unduly discriminatory or preferential; and (2) if not, what changes 
to the Tariff should be implemented as replacement rates.”). PJM and the Indicated PJM Transmission Owners filed 
their responses on March 24, 2025. Because NOVEC has filed these comments on April 23, 2025, it is timely.
